SUMMARY:Island Beach State Park
DESCRIPTION:One of the gems of the state park system\, Island Beach has miles of beach\, tidal wetlands\, maritime forest and thickets that can host a good diversity of birds\, especially if the winds are right. November sees peak numbers of migratory waterfowl\, loons\, gannets\, and other seabirds and is a good time of year for rarities. There is a $5 entry fee for NJ residents who do not have a state park pass or are 65 years of age or older. Be prepared for several hours of walking on flat terrain\, sometimes sandy. Bring lunch. Led by Scott Barnes and Linda Mack. \nA NOTE ON MEETING LOCATION! We’ll meet just outside of the park entrance\, in the median parking lot at the end of Rt. 35. \nPRE-REGISTRATION REQUIRED \nCOST: $25 Members\, $30 Non-members \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://njaudubon.org/event/island-beach-state-park-22/
LOCATION:NJ\, United States
CATEGORIES:All Things Birds,Bird Walk,Birding
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://njaudubon.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Island-Beach-State-Park-Nov-26.webp
END:VEVENT
